Wait: setLogger in try/finally? If an assertion throws... the expect is AFTER setLogger() reset, so no leak. But if one of the `await ...send` throws unexpectedly, setLogger stays stubbed for later tests. Put the sends in try/finally with setLogger() in finally. Acceptance test does setLogger in beforeEach and afterEach. Here I'll wrap:

```ts
setLogger({...});
try {
  await ...
} finally {
  setLogger();
}
```

Logger's setLogger signature — check src/shared/logger.ts to get exact param types. The acceptance test passes `{debug, info, warn, error}` where error takes (category, message, fields?). Let me verify quickly.

Also `logs` records only error level in my stub; fine.

One more consideration — `no-nondeterministic-tests` and `max-expects` satisfied. `require-spec-link` needs the citation.

Also — does the harness's ws mock need `readyState`? handleListSessions doesn't check readyState (non-lock path). answerInTurn checks but we're not in it. OK.

